y storage, then resolve neighbor IDs once through an open-addressed first-match map while retaining input order.\", \"Preselect each node's neighbor using the original zero initial maximum, strict greater-than comparison, first-on-ties behavior, missing-ID handling, and -1 recursion sentinel.\", \"Replace repeated recursive recomputation with demand-driven memoized evaluation over an explicit path stack; preserve root tokens and six-decimal output formatting.\"]}}, {\"id\": \"5acdcc28f0964695\", \"role\": \"A\", \"commit\": \"406fd8bca268a21ddd7dde42600c827f50f1b301\", \"mean_seconds\": 0.005705987413724263, \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/graph.c\"], \"retained\": [\"Store each node's value in its sorted ID/index lookup record so edge scans read neighbor metadata and value together.\", \"Resolve every requested root to its first input-order node index before releasing the lookup table.\", \"Preserve original node-order values for memoized path evaluation and retain the existing flattened, input-order edge storage.\"]}}, {\"id\": \"d62c996c67264658\", \"role\": \"C\", \"commit\": \"4a1edf068e825fe239a11e193d1c045ed3e51b46\", \"mean_seconds\": 0.010212274578710398, \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/graph.c\"], \"retained\": [\"Evaluate each requested node by iteratively walking its selected successor chain and accumulating values in reverse path order.\", \"Use dynamic OpenMP scheduling with one-request chunks only when both graph size and request count exceed general granularity thresholds; keep smaller workloads serial.\"]}}, {\"id\": \"9884f16ced4e43fb\", \"role\": \"B\", \"commit\": \"432e92656a1bf6b8540d73664b9b3583c7ed5c7d\", \"mean_seconds\": 0.010650597512722015, \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/graph.c\"], \"retained\": [\"Replace the full-scan OpenMP SIMD minimum reduction in find_by_id with a scalar loop that returns immediately on the first matching ID; retain the packed ID array and all other behavior.\"]}}, {\"id\": \"9d3fbdc2c73445ce\", \"role\": \"C\", \"commit\": \"6968ce1ae8d8ac577e1a412d4a2735565fec8829\", \"mean_seconds\": 0.011818882698814074, \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/graph.c\"], \"retained\": [\"Parse requested node IDs before computation and store their original tokens for output.\", \"For batches of at least four requests, evaluate each independent recursive search with an OpenMP parallel-for using dynamic one-item scheduling; retain serial evaluation for smaller batches.\", \"Buffer computed values and print them serially in request order.\"]}}, {\"id\": \"1cec78b84e3047bc\", \"role\": \"B\", \"commit\": \"a3282eaab40752cff4facc5ac99b5eab692e8b93\", \"mean_seconds\": 0.014670813456177711, \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/graph.c\"], \"retained\": [\"Express find_by_id's scan as an OpenMP SIMD loop with a min reduction; use the earliest matching index to retain existing lookup semantics.\", \"Restore valid line scans and guard zero-length graph allocation and empty neighbor lists.\"]}}]}, \"target_as_data\": {\"architecture\": \"ARM64\", \"cpu_cores\": 4, \"gpus\": 0}, \"required_schema\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"analysis\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"A\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"B\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"C\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"G\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"analysis\", \"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"G\"]}}",
